{"author":"John Wesley","book":"Notes on the Bible","chapter":749,"classification":{"bucket":"Christian Classics / Commentaries","canonicalStatus":"noncanonical","contentKind":"commentary","cautionReason":"","doctrinalStatus":"historical","labels":["christian-classics","commentaries"],"severity":0},"id":"classics:wesley:Ps.12","lineage":[],"metadata":{"author":"John Wesley","authorshipDateRange":"18th century","genre":"Commentaries","tradition":"Methodist","translator":null,"edition":"CCEL edition; source omits 2 Samuel 24","rights":"Public Domain","source":{"id":"wesley","provider":"CCEL","sourceUrl":"https://www.ccel.org/ccel/wesley/notes.html","title":"Notes on the Bible"}},"originalBook":"Psalms","sourceVolumeId":"wesley","source":{"id":"wesley","sourceUrl":"https://www.ccel.org/ccel/wesley/notes.html","title":"Notes on the Bible"},"title":"Psalms 12","reference":"Psalms 12","notes":[],"verses":[{"verse":1,"text":"David begs help of God, having no man whom he could trust, ver."},{"verse":2,"text":"1, 2."},{"verse":3,"text":"Describes the wicked and assures himself, that God would punish them, and preserve the just, ver."},{"verse":4,"text":"3-8."},{"verse":5,"text":"To the chief musician upon Sheminith, A psalm of David."},{"verse":6,"text":"Title of the psalm."},{"verse":7,"text":"Sheminith - The same title is prefixed to chap. vi, 1."},{"verse":8,"text":"4.","scriptureVerseStart":4,"scriptureVerseEnd":4},{"verse":9,"text":"Prevail - By raising and spreading evil reports concerning him.","scriptureVerseStart":4,"scriptureVerseEnd":4},{"verse":10,"text":"Our own - At our own disposal to speak what we please, who can control or restrain us?","scriptureVerseStart":4,"scriptureVerseEnd":4},{"verse":11,"text":"5.","scriptureVerseStart":5,"scriptureVerseEnd":5},{"verse":12,"text":"Puffeth - From him that despises him, and hopes to destroy him with a puff of breath.","scriptureVerseStart":5,"scriptureVerseEnd":5},{"verse":13,"text":"6.","scriptureVerseStart":6,"scriptureVerseEnd":6},{"verse":14,"text":"Pure - Without the least mixture of falsehood; and therefore shall infallibly be fulfilled.","scriptureVerseStart":6,"scriptureVerseEnd":6},{"verse":15,"text":"7.","scriptureVerseStart":7,"scriptureVerseEnd":7},{"verse":16,"text":"Thou shalt keep them - Thy words or promises: these thou wilt observe and keep, both now, and from this generation forever.","scriptureVerseStart":7,"scriptureVerseEnd":7},{"verse":17,"text":"8.","scriptureVerseStart":7,"scriptureVerseEnd":7},{"verse":18,"text":"Walk - They fill all places, and go about boldly and securely.","scriptureVerseStart":7,"scriptureVerseEnd":7}],"scriptureReference":{"book":"Psalms","chapter":12}}